From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Will Faust <willtechnoduck@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 28 Aug 2026 21:00:46 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] Fix the cycle detector reporting every multi-node list as
 cyclic

The tortoise and hare both started at the head and both advanced on the first
step, so after one record they compared equal and any list of two or more
nodes returned WMTW_PACK_CYCLE. Every real batch would have failed
immediately. The tortoise now advances on alternate steps only.

The bug survived a green 63-check suite because none of those checks called
wmtw_pack_render at all -- they exercised a private walker in the test. The
new suite drives the real packer over empty, single, two-node acyclic, 500-node
acyclic, self-cycle, two-node cycle and a 300-node ring, and asserts an
unsupported opcode is named with its opcode and record index.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01M1HvfVX2Y29TgJbFWbahdt
Madeira-commit: 107d4e1a327ded3766428e7c7ac583fa8c07992b
Rebased: clean
Class: madeira-port
Evidence: docs/evidence/2026-09-24-dxmt-latest-rebase.md
Offered-upstream: no
---
 src/winemetal/unix/wmt_remote_pack.h | 9 +++++++--
 1 file changed, 7 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/src/winemetal/unix/wmt_remote_pack.h b/src/winemetal/unix/wmt_remote_pack.h
index 2bc72a1..290b4ea 100644
--- a/src/winemetal/unix/wmt_remote_pack.h
+++ b/src/winemetal/unix/wmt_remote_pack.h
@@ -25,7 +25,12 @@ static inline enum wmtw_pack_status
 wmtw_pack_render(const struct wmtcmd_base *head, struct wmtw_packer *p,
                  struct wmtw_pack_result *res)
 {
+    /* Tortoise and hare. The tortoise must NOT advance on the first step:
+     * starting both at head and advancing both immediately makes them equal
+     * after one step, which reports every list of two or more nodes as
+     * cyclic. */
     const struct wmtcmd_base *slow = head;
+    int advance_slow = 0;
     uint32_t idx = 0;
     res->encoder_kind = 0;
 
@@ -152,8 +157,8 @@ wmtw_pack_render(const struct wmtcmd_base *head, struct wmtw_packer *p,
 
         c = (const struct wmtcmd_base *)c->next.ptr;
         idx++;
-        /* Floyd: advance the slow pointer every other step. */
-        if (idx & 1) { if (slow) slow = (const struct wmtcmd_base *)slow->next.ptr; }
+        if (advance_slow && slow) slow = (const struct wmtcmd_base *)slow->next.ptr;
+        advance_slow = !advance_slow;
         if (c && c == slow) { res->status = WMTW_PACK_CYCLE; res->record_index = idx;
                               res->opcode = c->type; return WMTW_PACK_CYCLE; }
     }
